WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:20.568
Describe rhythm along two axes: where the impulse originates and how it conducts. A sinus origin does not guarantee normal AV conduction, and a narrow QRS does not identify the atrial pacemaker. Use the six steps to establish each feature instead of jumping from one visual clue to a label.
从两个维度描述节律：激动起源在哪里，如何传导。窦性起源不保证房室传导正常，窄 QRS 也不能确定心房起搏点。应利用六步法分别建立证据，不要从单个外观直接跳到名称。

00:00:20.568 --> 00:00:38.880
For the reference sinus pattern, look for a consistent upright P before each QRS in lead two, one-to-one conduction, a regular rate in the adult teaching range and appropriate intervals. This is a reference pattern, not proof that the patient has no cardiac disease.
参考窦性形态应在 II 导联看到每个 QRS 前有一致向上 P 波、一对一传导、成人教学范围内的规则心率及合适间期。这是参考形态，不是患者没有心脏疾病的证明。

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:59.640
Sinus bradycardia preserves the sinus relationships but has a rate below sixty. Causes include conditioning, vagal effects, hypothermia, hypoxia, nodal ischemia and medication effects. Assess symptoms and perfusion; the rhythm-classification cutoff is not automatically a treatment trigger.
窦性心动过缓保留窦性关系，但频率低于每分钟60次。原因包括体能适应、迷走作用、低温、缺氧、结区缺血及药物。应评估症状与灌注；节律分类界值不自动成为治疗触发点。

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:21.768
Sinus tachycardia is above one hundred with the same sinus pattern. Look for pain, fever, hypovolemia, hypoxia, anxiety, pulmonary illness or stimulants. Reducing a compensatory rate without correcting the cause can worsen output. A fast number alone does not establish re-entry SVT.
窦性心动过速是在相同窦性形态下频率超过100。应寻找疼痛、发热、低血容量、缺氧、焦虑、肺部疾病或兴奋剂。未纠正原因就压低代偿性心率，可能使输出恶化；单凭心率快不能确定折返性 SVT。

00:01:21.768 --> 00:01:41.256
Respiratory sinus arrhythmia produces cyclic rate variation, commonly in younger people, while the P-to-QRS relationship remains sinus. Confirm the pattern rather than calling every irregular rhythm AF. Not all irregularity has the same mechanism or urgency.
呼吸性窦性心律不齐表现为周期性心率变化，年轻人较常见，同时保留窦性 P-QRS 关系。应确认模式，不能把所有不齐都叫房颤；不同不齐的机制与紧急性并不相同。

00:01:41.256 --> 00:02:01.896
A sinus pause or arrest presents a missing expected atrial impulse, sometimes followed by an escape beat. Review vagal influences, medication and sinus-node disease. Recurrent or symptomatic pauses merit urgent evaluation; a short strip may not establish the exact pause mechanism.
窦性停顿或停搏表现为预期心房激动缺失，有时继以逸搏。应复核迷走因素、药物及窦房结疾病。反复或伴症状的停顿需要紧急评估，而短条带未必能确定确切机制。

00:02:01.896 --> 00:02:21.000
A premature atrial contraction starts early from an atrial focus outside the sinus node. Look for an early P with a different shape; it may be partly hidden in the preceding T wave. The following QRS is often narrow but may be aberrant or absent if conduction fails.
房性早搏来自窦房结之外的心房灶，提前出现。应寻找提前且形态不同的 P 波，有时部分藏在前一 T 波中。随后 QRS 常较窄，但也可能差异传导，或因未下传而缺失。

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:42.888
Assess frequency, change from baseline and the patient rather than treating one isolated PAC as an emergency. Stress, caffeine, electrolyte disturbance and structural disease are possible associations. Frequent atrial ectopy may justify closer observation and follow-up without proving AF on that strip.
应评估频率、相对基线变化及患者状况，而不是把一个孤立房早当急症。压力、咖啡因、电解质异常及结构病变均可能有关。频发房性异位活动可促使加强观察和随访，但不等于该条带已证明房颤。

00:02:42.888 --> 00:03:04.392
Wandering atrial pacemaker shows changing P-wave shapes as the dominant atrial focus shifts. At least three distinct P morphologies support the school pattern. When that multifocal atrial pattern is tachycardic, above one hundred per minute, it is called multifocal atrial tachycardia rather than simple wandering pacemaker.
游走性心房起搏表现为优势心房灶转移、P 波形态变化，学校以至少三种不同 P 形态作为支持。相同多源心房形态在频率超过每分钟100次、属于心动过速时，称多源性房性心动过速，而不是单纯游走性起搏。

00:03:04.392 --> 00:03:26.424
MAT can be associated with significant pulmonary disease and metabolic stress. Unlike AF, discernible P waves with multiple shapes are present. Compare multiple beats, assess oxygenation and physiology, and communicate the rhythm and underlying illness rather than assuming one universal rate-control solution.
MAT 可见于显著肺病和代谢应激。它与房颤不同，存在可辨认但形态多样的 P 波。应比较多个搏动，评估氧合与生理状态，并报告节律及基础病，不能假定只有一种通用控速方案。

00:03:26.424 --> 00:03:45.984
Atrial flutter is organized rapid atrial activity, often with a sawtooth appearance in inferior leads. The school reference is an atrial rate around two hundred fifty to three hundred fifty. Count atrial and ventricular activity separately because not every atrial impulse conducts.
心房扑动是快速但有组织的心房活动，常在下壁导联呈锯齿样。学校参考心房率约每分钟250至350次。应分别计算心房和心室活动，因为不是每次心房激动都下传。

00:03:45.984 --> 00:04:07.920
With fixed conduction, the ventricular rhythm may be very regular; with changing conduction, it may vary. Flutter waves can hide in QRS or T waves. Structural and valvular disease or pulmonary illness may contribute. Urgency depends on perfusion and symptoms, not on seeing a sawtooth alone.
传导比例固定时，心室节律可非常规则；比例变化时则可能不齐。扑动波可藏在 QRS 或 T 波内。结构、瓣膜病或肺部疾病可能相关，紧急性取决于灌注和症状，不是只看锯齿。

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:27.624
Atrial fibrillation combines disorganized atrial activity with an irregularly irregular ventricular response when AV conduction is variable. Look for the absence of consistent discrete P waves across a sufficient sample. Noise or a single irregular interval is not enough evidence.
房颤由无组织心房活动与房室下传变化造成的 RR 绝对不齐组成。应在足够长记录中寻找一致、离散 P 波的缺失；噪声或一个不规则间期不是充分证据。

00:04:27.624 --> 00:04:49.752
AF can reduce coordinated atrial contribution and may carry thromboembolic risk. Obtain onset and medication history when feasible. If the patient is unstable, seek urgent authorized care; the school shorthand about rate control must not be read as permission for a PCP to choose antiarrhythmic treatment independently.
房颤可削弱协调心房充盈贡献，并可能伴血栓栓塞风险。可行时取得发作时间和用药史。若患者不稳定，应紧急取得授权救治；不能把学校关于控速的简写理解为 PCP 可自主选择抗心律失常治疗。

00:04:49.752 --> 00:05:09.048
The school describes PSVT as typically narrow, regular and very rapid with abrupt onset and offset, often without easily visible P waves. The rate may exceed one hundred fifty, but that number alone does not distinguish SVT from sinus tachycardia or flutter.
学校把 PSVT 描述为常见窄、规则、非常快，突然开始或终止，且 P 波往往不易看见。频率可能超过150，但该数值本身不能把 SVT 与窦速、房扑区分开。

00:05:09.048 --> 00:05:30.336
Ask how it started, inspect atrial activity and look for a cause of compensatory tachycardia. Vagal manoeuvres and medicines require the applicable service pathway and authority; do not turn a recognition lecture into a treatment order. Instability requires urgent escalation, not prolonged naming exercises.
应询问起病方式、查看心房活动并寻找代偿性心动过速原因。迷走操作和药物须符合机构流程及权限，不能把识别课变成治疗医嘱。不稳定时须紧急升级救治，而不是长时间练习命名。

00:05:30.336 --> 00:05:46.392
Organize causes into autonomic, structural, metabolic and medication-related groups. This helps connect the history to the tracing and prevents a rhythm label from ending assessment. The same named rhythm can have different causes in two patients.
可把原因分为自主神经、结构性、代谢性和药物相关四组，从病史连接到波形，避免说出节律名称后就停止评估。两名患者的同名节律可有不同原因。

00:05:46.392 --> 00:06:09.384
Check for altered mentation, shock signs, ischemic discomfort and serious respiratory compromise. Decide whether the rhythm is causing deterioration or is a response to another problem. Recognition here supports monitoring, communication and escalation; detailed treatment decisions are the later ECG 201 scope.
应检查意识变化、休克征象、缺血性不适和严重呼吸问题，并判断节律是在引起恶化，还是另一问题的反应。本课识别用于监护、沟通和升级；详细治疗决策属于后续 ECG 201 范围。
